D. ACCURATE COUNTING

Views must represent genuine, validated viewing activity.

Do not increase views because of:

- Automatic page refreshes.
- Component rerendering.
- Background synchronisation.
- Repeated API requests for the same displayed post.
- Opening a feed that never actually displays the post.
- Repeatedly refreshing the same content.

Design a sensible view-counting policy.

Deduplicate repeated views within a defined user, device or viewing-session window where technically appropriate.

Explain the selected counting policy in your final report.

Do not artificially inflate view counts.

E. LIVE COUNT UPDATES

View counts should update through the website's existing background update system without forcing a page reload.

